<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    RDR-192 Step 2 round-2 fix (bead nexus-wbfpw.4, code-review Important) —
    partial expression index serving the "nl3fn NOTES GUARD" reverse-lookup
    predicate, which had no index anywhere in the schema.

    Two independent sites correlate on this exact predicate today:
      - CatalogRepository.sweepChunksQuery's "nl3fn NOTES GUARD"
        (production's own reap-time protection for a live manifest-less
        note — CatalogRepository.java ~5927-5946).
      - PgVectorRepository.MANIFEST_LESS_CENSUS_SQL's reverse-owner LATERAL
        (scripts/sql/manifest_less_census.sql, byte-identical), added in
        this bead's round-1 fix to classify the same row class.

    Both express the IDENTICAL five-predicate join: tenant_id,
    physical_collection, deleted_at IS NULL (live), file_path IS NULL OR ''
    (note-shaped), metadata->>'doc_id' = a chash hex string. The base scan (nexus.chunks
    by its own PK) and the forward-owner join (catalog_documents_pk) are
    both already index-backed; this is the one leg of the census query —
    and of production's own sweep — that is genuinely correlated on the
    OUTER row's chash and cannot be hoisted out of a per-row lookup, so it
    runs an unindexed scan over every live, note-shaped catalog_documents
    row in the collection for every manifest-less/dead-forward-owner chunk
    it considers. Not a live problem at today's measured population
    (~147 manifest-less rows total, per the round-1 review), but Step 3b
    widens the census to every non-quarantine collection and Step 9 ships
    an hourly reaper leaning on the same notes-guard shape at a much
    higher cadence — code-review round-2 finding, not ship-blocking for
    this bead alone but landed here since it directly serves the SQL this
    bead just wrote.

    Partial + expression index, matching this repo's established
    conventions for the SAME table (catalog-016-1's partial unique index
    on (tenant_id, source_uri) WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND source_uri
    &lt;&gt; '' is the direct precedent for a partial index scoped to LIVE
    rows on catalog_documents): the predicate columns are (tenant_id,
    physical_collection, (metadata ->> 'doc_id')), narrowed by the WHERE
    clause to exactly the row population the notes guard and the reverse
    LATERAL both restrict to (deleted_at IS NULL, note-shaped). A
    non-partial index would waste space indexing every non-note and
    tombstoned document this predicate can never match.

    Plain CREATE INDEX, not CONCURRENTLY — matching vectors-003's
    documented BUILD-WINDOW DECISION for this exact class of choice
    (chash-probe indexes on chunks_384/768/1024, RDR-187 bead
    nexus-piwya.1): Liquibase runs in the boot-time migration window
    before the engine serves traffic; catalog_documents is smaller than
    the chunks tables that decision was made against (~255k chunk rows
    post-RDR-180 rekey at the time), so a two-column-plus-expression
    partial btree here builds even faster; and CONCURRENTLY would need
    runInTransaction="false" and can strand an INVALID index on a failed
    build, which plain CREATE INDEX inside the changeset transaction
    cannot — it is valid-or-absent. No precondition/MARK_RAN gate: unlike
    vectors-003's target (a table plausibly pre-built out-of-band by an
    operator script at very large scale), nothing in this codebase creates
    this index ahead of Liquibase, so the ordinary checksum/idempotency
    guarantee is enough.

    Purely additive DDL (CREATE INDEX, no row ever changes) — no DATA
    EFFECT line needed per scripts/data_effect_lint.py's own documented
    scope ("A purely additive changeset (CREATE, ADD COLUMN, ADD
    CONSTRAINT, CREATE INDEX, GRANT, VALIDATE CONSTRAINT, ...) needs
    nothing").

    Plan-shape proof: ManifestLessCensusNotesGuardIndexPlanShapeTest
    EXPLAINs MANIFEST_LESS_CENSUS_SQL against a seeded population (5,000
    live note-shaped catalog_documents rows in one collection) and asserts
    the reverse LATERAL binds to this index rather than seq-scanning
    catalog_documents.

    Placed after catalog-037-gc-quarantine-orphans-bounded.xml (current
    tail in the catalog-NNN series at authoring time) and before the
    grants-nexus-svc.xml runAlways block, matching the established
    late-append convention.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="catalog-038-1" author="nexus-wbfpw.4">
        <comment>idx_catalog_documents_live_note_doc_id: partial expression index on nexus.catalog_documents (tenant_id, physical_collection, (metadata-&gt;&gt;'doc_id')) WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND (file_path IS NULL OR file_path = '') -- serves CatalogRepository.sweepChunksQuery's "nl3fn NOTES GUARD" and PgVectorRepository.MANIFEST_LESS_CENSUS_SQL's reverse-owner LATERAL, the two sites that resolve a live manifest-less note by its own metadata.doc_id identity chash.</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="true">
CREATE INDEX idx_catalog_documents_live_note_doc_id
    ON nexus.catalog_documents (tenant_id, physical_collection, (metadata ->> 'doc_id'))
 WHERE deleted_at IS NULL AND (file_path IS NULL OR file_path = '');
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql>DROP INDEX IF EXISTS nexus.idx_catalog_documents_live_note_doc_id;</sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
